<title>USA: Favorable harvest weather for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>Favorable harvest weather for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure in Brazil's coffee belt is expected to remain in place preventing any cold air from moving into the area, Weather Services Corp said an update on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed in main growing areas of the belt this morning. Temperatures were slightly below normal with lows dipping into the 50's F (low teens C). Some higher elevations reported temperatures in the 40's F (7-9 C).   Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for the next seven days. Temperatures will stay near normal levels. Low temperatures should remain in the 50's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>&quot;There is no damaging cold expected as favorable harvest weather has returned.&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
